(:taskCollection
  :id "Phase465AgentWorkingMemorySurface"
  :createdAt 1789280000000
  :status "planned"
  :priorityOrder 2
  :summary "Agent Working Memory Surface: give the memory engine that already exists a command surface, a file worklist, a scope lifecycle, an instruction that an agent keeps notes, and a measurement of whether any of it helps."
  :phase "Phase465AgentWorkingMemorySurface"
  :baseline "Researched 2026-09-12 and recorded in D81PersistentMemoryResearch20260912. The engine exists and executes: notes with scope, tags, query and promotion to task or decision at 25 assertions, session leases at 100, crash recovery with resume-action-dag and handoff extraction at 86, amnesia at 26, plus pointer offloading with should-offload? and total-active-tokens, tiered paging with eviction, context scoring that penalises unreferenced matches, BM25 retrieval over the spool, and a deferred PostActionQueue. Nothing can call any of it: asl task, asl note and asl doctor are absent by direct invocation; the string note occurs zero times in asl/grammar/rules.asn and zero times in AGENTS.md; the modules are among the 270 that no import reaches; mem/tests/tasks_test.asl exits 1 with zero assertions and mem/tests/checkpoint_test.asl fails with ERR_UNBOUND_SYMBOL; and InFlight.asn has carried an empty active list since it was created. No structure anywhere holds a list of files with a per entry done mark."
  :tasks [
    (:task
      :id "Task46501"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "A command surface over the memory that already works"
      :kind :tooling
      :state :planned
      :lane "surface"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "Two hundred and thirty seven assertions of tested working memory machinery have zero users, because no command reaches them. This is the cheapest large improvement available in the repository: the engineering is done, tested and passing, and the missing part is the door. Building a second memory system instead would be the expensive way to get less."
      :purpose "Commands expose what the modules already provide: write and query a note, open and claim a task, enqueue and drain a deferred action, snapshot and resume a session. The surface is thin by construction, adding no logic of its own, so the tested behaviour is the shipped behaviour and a defect is in one place."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Notes, tasks, queue and recovery reachable from a session" "The surface adds no logic beyond dispatch" "The four commands the project instruction already mandates exist or are withdrawn" "237 passing assertions acquire a caller"]
      :owns ["asl/tools/asl.c" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn" "mem/src/tasks.asl"]
      :targetSymbols ["make-note" "note-matches-query?" "task-claim-session" "post-action-enqueue" "recover-task-session"]
      :relatedSymbols ["anchor" "capabilities" "tools"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D46" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46402"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46501"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46501.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A note written through the command is found by a query through the command in a later process." "A claimed task is refused to a second claimant while the lease holds and granted after it expires." "The surface contains no branch that the module tests do not already cover, checked by removing the module and observing the command fail rather than degrade."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46501" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
