    (:task
      :id "Task46502"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "A file worklist with a per entry mark, walked by cursor"
      :kind :language
      :state :planned
      :lane "worklist"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "The scout workflow is to enumerate a package and then walk the enumeration, and there is nowhere to put the enumeration. A search across the whole memory package for a worklist, a file queue, a to-visit list or an inspected mark found only graph traversal visited sets. So the list lives in context, which is precisely the thing that decays: measured here, a retrieved slice is frequently separated from what defines it, with the ninetieth percentile of binding distance at 232 lines."
      :purpose "A worklist holds entries, each an intent against a path with a status of pending, reading, done or skipped, a reason where skipped, and room for what was found. It is walked by a cursor that yields a bounded batch, so the caller holds a batch and the list holds the rest, and the cursor survives a process ending. Batch size is chosen per walk rather than fixed, since a scout reading outlines and an implementer editing files want different sizes."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A worklist with per entry status and finding" "A cursor yielding bounded batches" "The cursor survives process death" "Batch size chosen per walk"]
      :owns ["mem/src" "asl/grammar/rpc.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["PostActionQueue" "post-action-enqueue" "post-action-drain"]
      :relatedSymbols ["bounded" "budget" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["C3" "D46" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46501"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46502"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46502.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["A walk interrupted midway resumes at the first pending entry and never re-yields a done one." "Two walkers over one list do not receive the same entry." "An entry marked skipped without a reason is rejected, so the list cannot be drained by marking."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46502" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the entry and its states." "Build the cursor on the existing queue." "Persist and resume." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46503"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "Scope means something: step, task, epic, and what retires a note"
      :kind :protocol
      :state :planned
      :lane "scope"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "Notes already carry a scope field and a scope matcher, and nothing defines the scopes or says what happens when one closes. Without that, a note store either grows without bound until retrieval is as expensive as the context it replaced, or is cleared by hand and loses the thing worth keeping. The modules for both halves exist: context scoring penalises unreferenced matches and amnesia implements deliberate forgetting."
      :purpose "Three scopes are defined by lifetime rather than by size: a step note dies with its step, a task note with its task, and an epic note outlives both and is what a later session inherits. Closing a scope promotes what is still true and retires the rest, using the existing promotion path into a task or a decision, so nothing worth keeping is lost by a deletion and nothing else survives by accident."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["Three scopes defined by lifetime" "Closing a scope promotes or retires each note" "Retrieval cost bounded by construction" "Promotion uses the path that already exists"]
      :owns ["mem/src/notes.asl" "mem/src/amnesia.asl" ".asl/mem/notes.asn"]
      :targetSymbols ["note-scope-matches?" "note-promote-to-task" "note-promote-to-adr" "evict-below-threshold"]
      :relatedSymbols ["budget" "context" "anchor"]
      :invariants ["D46" "D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46501"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46503"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46503.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["Closing a step retires its step notes and leaves its task notes." "A note promoted at scope close is retrievable after the scope is gone." "A store under continuous writing stays bounded, measured rather than asserted."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46503" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the three lifetimes." "Wire close to promote or retire." "Measure boundedness." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46504"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "Tell the agent the memory exists, and why rather than when"
      :kind :protocol
      :state :planned
      :lane "surface"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "The word note appears zero times in the rule source and zero times in the rendered agent instructions. An agent is never told that an external memory exists, so the best possible implementation would still have no users. The anchor rule already concedes this in its own text, telling the reader to keep the plan in the task file until the ledger ops exist."
      :purpose "The rule source gains one rule, rendered to every client through the existing single source: what the agent is holding in context that it would lose, it writes down, and it decides what to write rather than being given a checklist. The rule states the conditions the note must survive, being the task, what was asked, the expected result, the steps as separate items, the files with their marks and the findings, and leaves the judgement of what matters to the agent. It is expressed as a reason, not a procedure, because a procedure is followed until it is forgotten and a reason is reconstructed."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["One rule in the single source, rendered everywhere" "The agent decides what to record" "Conditions and expected results survive outside context" "The anchor rule concession retired"]
      :owns ["asl/grammar/rules.asn" "scripts/install.sh" "AGENTS.md"]
      :targetSymbols ["anchor" "budget"]
      :relatedSymbols ["ssot" "anchor" "context" "budget"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46501" "Task46401"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46504"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46504.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The rendered surface for every client contains the rule, checked by the existing drift gate." "The rule names only commands that exist, checked by Task46401." "The rule states a reason and not a fixed list of fields, so a task needing a field nobody anticipated is still served."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46504" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Write the rule in the single source." "Render and check drift." "Retire the anchor concession." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])
    (:task
      :id "Task46505"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "Repair the facade and the checkpoint suite the engine rests on"
      :kind :remediation
      :state :planned
      :lane "surface"
      :priority :high
      :ownerRole "implementer"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "The sub-modules pass and the facade over them does not: mem/tests/tasks_test.asl exits 1 having executed zero assertions, and mem/tests/checkpoint_test.asl fails with ERR_UNBOUND_SYMBOL. A command surface built on an unverified facade would inherit an unverified path, and a zero assertion exit is indistinguishable from a suite that never ran."
      :purpose "Both suites execute and their assertions run, so the facade the command surface dispatches through is covered rather than assumed. The zero assertion case is treated as a failure in its own right, not as an incidental exit code."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["The facade suite executes with non zero assertions" "The checkpoint suite binds and runs" "A zero assertion exit treated as failure"]
      :owns ["mem/src/tasks.asl" "mem/src/checkpoint.asl" "mem/tests"]
      :targetSymbols ["make-task" "create-vfs-checkpoint" "restore-vfs-checkpoint"]
      :relatedSymbols ["semantics" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
