    (:task
      :id "Task46506"
      :parentId ""
      :phase "phase-465"
      :title "Measure whether keeping notes actually helps"
      :kind :verification
      :state :planned
      :lane "effect"
      :priority :critical
      :ownerRole "verifier"
      :createdAt 1789280000000
      :updatedAt 1789280000000
      :motivation "The expected benefits are fewer hallucinations and better sustained attention, and both are currently hypotheses. This project has already produced one confident token economy conclusion that its own direct measurement reversed, and an unmeasured memory system is exactly the kind of thing that feels effective while costing tool calls. The instrument exists in the plan: a fixed task set with a measured emission error rate."
      :purpose "The same fixed task set runs with note keeping available and withheld, across the same models, and the difference is recorded as a rate rather than an impression: unsupported claims about the codebase, steps dropped from a stated plan, files re-read after being read, and tasks completed. A negative or null result is recorded as such and the feature is judged on it."
      :context (:contractRef D81PlanContext)
      :outcomes ["A measured difference with and without notes" "Unsupported claims and dropped steps counted, not estimated" "A null result recorded and acted on" "The cost in tool calls counted against the benefit"]
      :owns ["asl/bench" ".asl/mem/telemetry"]
      :targetSymbols []
      :relatedSymbols ["concepts" "grading" "gates"]
      :invariants ["D81"]
      :variations (:contractRef D81SettledChoices)
      :failureModes (:contractRef D81TaskFailureModes)
      :additionalRequirements (:contractRef D81Ownership)
      :adr "ADR-0081"
      :decision "d81"
      :dependsOn ["Task46504" "Task46304"]
      :gate "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46506"
      :acceptanceCriteria (:contractRef D81BehavioralAcceptance)
      :contractRefs [D81PlanContext D81SettledChoices D81TaskFailureModes D81BehavioralAcceptance D81Baseline D81Ownership D81Receipts]
      :verificationRole "independentVerifier"
      :verificationOwns ["tests/acceptance/d81/Task46506.asl"]
      :verificationCases ["The two arms differ only in the availability of the memory surface." "An unsupported claim is counted by checking it against the tree, not by judging it." "A null result passes the gate and is recorded, so the measurement cannot only confirm."]
      :gateReadiness :requiresIndependentBaseline
      :baselineProbe (:command "sh tests/acceptance/d81/SuperviseGate.sh Task46506" :status :notEstablished :contract D81Baseline)
      :historicalReceipts []
      :reviewStatus :requiresIndependentPlanReview
      :actionDag ["Define the counted outcomes." "Run both arms on the fixed set." "Record the difference and the cost." "Independent acceptance."]
      :stepIndex 0
      :receipts [])]
  :notes "The research finding that shapes this phase is that the engine is built and passing and has no door. Building a second memory system would cost more and deliver less than opening the one that exists. The worked scout example is in docs/EXAMPLE_DOCTRINE.md.")
